ot of the upcoming mission  impossible dead reckoning part 1 will  look like as usual with the franchise  little is revealed about the exact  storyline beforehand so our best clue is  the first trailer which was released at  the end of may in the barely 2 minute  long piece of action we see some  well-known faces including ethan hunt's  imf team consisting of ilsa benji and  luther clearly more exciting though is  the reunion between hunt and former imf  chief eugene kittridge the two last met  in the very first mission impossible  film and that was no less than 26 years  ago even then kittrich was wary of ethan  hunt and although hunt was able to clear  his name kid rich vanished from the  movie series altogether in the trailer  scene the two again seem to have a  rather strained relationship the former  imf director confronts hunt with a  question whether his loyalty is to the  us government or to his personal ideals  a further indication of a conflict  between hunt and the imf can be found in  the scene in which kidridge and an older  men sit across from each other in what  maybe ethan hunt in disguise the latter  throws two gas bombs into the room  knocking everyone unconscious about  himself in kittridge this could be a  sign that the imf is once again engaged  in dubious schemes and it appears to be  the only way han can have an undisturbed  talk with the imf official another  storyline will be the relationship  between hunt and elsa faust the tough  female agent has been an integral part  of the film series since mission  impossible 5 rogue nation and has also  been a potential love interest for the  main character ever since in the trailer  we see the two of them happily embracing  but also some sequences where they can  be spotted with an eye patch and blonde  hair also in one scene she seems to have  a heated argument with hunt suggesting a  volatile relationship between the two  further she wears a cross-like key  around her neck this could be an  importa